---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import LmwfCode from '../../components/LmwfCode.astro';

const minimalExample = `# Bench Day
@units: lbs

## Bench Press
- 135 x 5
- 185 x 5
- 225 x 5
`;

const richExample = `# Push Day
@tags: strength, push
@units: lbs

Focus on bar path on bench. Keep rest strict — don't pad between sets. Stop if bar speed dies on the top set.

## Warmup

### Band Pull-Aparts
- x 20

### Light Bench Press
- 45 x 10
- 95 x 5

## Bench Press

Build to a top set, then back off. Stop the top set if bar speed dies — no grinders.

- 135 x 5 @rest: 120s
- 185 x 5 @rest: 180s
- 225 x 5 @rest: 180s Aim for RPE 7
- 245 x 3 Target RPE 8, leave 2 in the tank

## Overhead Press

Strict press, no leg drive. If the last set feels easy, add 5 lbs next session.

- 95 x 8 @rest: 90s
- 115 x 8 @rest: 90s
- 135 x 6

## Arms Superset

### Cable Triceps Pushdown
- 50 x 12
- 50 x 12
- 50 x 10

### Dumbbell Curl
- 30 x 10
- 30 x 10
- 30 x 8

## Cooldown

### Chest Stretch
- 60s

### Foam Rolling
- 2m
`;

// "The format as brand" code blocks use the shared <LmwfCode> widget so the
// token coloring stays consistent across the site (format hub, agents page, …).
---

<Base
  title="Format"
  description="The lift.md format — a markdown-based format for strength training workouts. Human-writable, machine-parseable, open spec."
  ogImage="/brand/social/og-liftmd.png"
  formatBrand
>
  <h1>lift.md format</h1>

  <p>
    lift.md format is a small, markdown-based format for strength training
    workouts (formerly "LMWF"). It is designed to be readable and editable by
    humans, and trivially parseable by tools — including LLMs asked to generate
    or modify workouts. The format is an open specification licensed under
    <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" rel="external noopener license">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>,
    independent of any particular app.
  </p>

  <p>
    At its simplest, a workout is a header, an exercise, and a list of sets:
  </p>

  <LmwfCode code={minimalExample} />

  <p>
    That's a valid lift.md format document. Most real programs need more —
    warmup and cooldown blocks, programming guidance, per-set rest targets,
    time-based sets, tags, and supersets. All of it stays in plain markdown:
  </p>

  <LmwfCode code={richExample} />

  <p>
    A lift.md format document describes a workout <em>plan</em> — what you
    intend to do, not a record of what happened. A few things to notice:
    <code>@tags</code> and <code>@units</code> are workout-level metadata;
    prose between a header and its sets is preserved as a note, and is the
    right place for programming intent, cues, and stop conditions (see the
    notes under <em>Push Day</em>, <em>Bench Press</em>, and
    <em>Overhead Press</em>); <code>@rest</code> is the main per-set
    modifier, and any trailing text after the set and its modifiers becomes
    a freeform note on that set — the preferred way to express descriptive
    targets like RPE or tempo; sets without a weight (<code>- x 20</code>)
    are bodyweight; sets expressed as a duration (<code>- 60s</code>,
    <code>- 2m</code>) are time-based; and <em>Arms Superset</em>
    demonstrates the superset convention — a parent header with its
    exercises nested one level deeper.
  </p>

  <p>
    See the <a href="/format/spec">full spec</a> for the complete set of
    modifiers, metadata fields, validation rules, and edge cases.
  </p>

  <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>

  <p>
    Edit or paste a lift.md format workout below and click Validate. The
    request is sent to the live validator API at <code>POST /validate</code>.
  </p>

  <form id="validator-form" novalidate>
    <label for="markdown" class="visually-hidden">lift.md format markdown</label>
    <textarea
      id="markdown"
      name="markdown"
      rows="20"
      wrap="soft"
      spellcheck="false"
      autocomplete="off"
      autocapitalize="off"
    >{richExample}</textarea>

    <div class="validator-actions">
      <button type="submit" id="validate-btn" class="lm-btn lm-btn-primary">Validate</button>
      <span id="validator-status" class="muted" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>
  </form>

  <div id="validator-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>

  <h2>Links</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="/format/spec">Full specification</a> (also available as <a href="/spec.md">raw markdown</a>)</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/vfilby/lift.md" rel="external noopener">GitHub repository</a></li>
    <li>
      Validator API: <code>POST https://getlift.md/validate</code>
      with JSON body <code>&#123;"markdown": "..."&#125;</code>
    </li>
    <li><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> — machine-readable index for LLMs</li>
  </ul>

  <style>
    /* The nav lockup (formatBrand) already carries the "lift.md format"
       wordmark, so keep the H1 for SEO/structure but visually hide it. */
    h1 {
      position: absolute;
      width: 1px; height: 1px;
      padding: 0; margin: -1px;
      overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
      white-space: nowrap; border: 0;
    }

    /* The lift.md "format as brand" code styling now lives in <LmwfCode>. */

    textarea {
      width: 100%;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: var(--lm-radius-md);
      background: var(--lm-code-bg);
      color: var(--lm-code-text);
      resize: vertical;
      min-height: 12rem;
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      word-break: break-word;
    }
    textarea:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 1px; }

    .validator-actions {
      margin-top: 0.75rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
    #validate-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: progress; }

    #validator-result { margin-top: 1rem; }

    .result {
      border-radius: var(--lm-radius-md);
      border: 1px solid;
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    }
    .result.ok {
      background: var(--color-ok-bg);
      color: var(--color-ok-fg);
      border-color: var(--color-ok-border);
    }
    .result.err {
      background: var(--color-err-bg);
      color: var(--color-err-fg);
      border-color: var(--color-err-border);
    }
    .result h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; }
    .result ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    .result dl {
      margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
      gap: 0.15rem 0.75rem;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
    .result dt { font-weight: 600; }
    .result dd { margin: 0; }

    .visually-hidden {
      position: absolute;
      width: 1px; height: 1px;
      padding: 0; margin: -1px;
      overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
      white-space: nowrap; border: 0;
    }
  </style>

  <!--
    Format-hub validator demo: external module (not `is:inline`) for CSP
    `script-src 'self'` compatibility. Astro bundles it to /_astro/*.js.
  -->
  <script>
    import '../../scripts/validator-form.js';
  </script>
</Base>
